 34S     4HE(30SI,A):RESONANCES        2011NO07                  ENSDF    202609
 34S   H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34S  c  J|p=0+ for {+30}Si ground state                                        
 34S  c  2011No07: 30Si+|a elastic scattering was studied using the Thick Target
 34S 2c  Inverse Kinematics technique. A 150-MeV {+30}Si beam was produced from 
 34S 3c  the K-130 cyclotron at the University of Jyvaskyla, Finland. The beam  
 34S 4c  entered scattering chamber filled with helium gas through a Havar foil.
 34S 5c  The recoiling |a particles were detected using an array of four silicon
 34S 6c  surface detectors. Measured E|a, I|a. Deduced excitation function,     
 34S 7c  levels, J, widths (|G), and partial widths (|G{-|a}/|G) using a        
 34S 8c  simplified R-matrix approach.                                          
 34S  cL E$2011No07 states that the uncertainty in the absolute energy          
 34S 2cL calibration is |?100 keV.                                              
 34S  cL T$Relative reduced widths=|g{+2}{-|a}/|g{+2}{-sp}, where |g{+2}{-|a} is
 34S 2cL the reduced |a width and |g{+2}{-sp} is the single-particle limit.     
 34S 3cL 2011No07 states that the reported total widths represent only an upper 
 34S 4cL limit, since most resonances are seen at about the experimental        
 34S 5cL resolution of 50 keV. |G{-|a}/|G is underestimated by 10% with 30%     
 34S 6cL uncertainty. |g{+2}{-|a}/|g{+2}{-sp} is overestimated by 30%. The      
 34S 7cL errors are usually larger than the mean error at low energies, and     
 34S 8cL smaller than the average at high energies.                             
